    {
      "title": "Encrypted Exchange",
      "desc": "HTTP inside TLS records",
      "detail": "The GET and 200 OK are the same HTTP messages as before, sealed in TLS records that look like random “application data” on the wire. The server also hands over two session tickets, so a later visit can skip part of the handshake.",
